<<~ ahu slot=`#/contract`>>

!! Contract

`stack[]` — emits each input carrier's qualified has-stack URIs, deduped: relative tags qualify against the carrier's OWN bag scope (`root/@bag/version` from its title); `lar:` tags pass through; system and free-form tags ride outside the stack.

`stack:has[X]` — keeps carriers whose stack holds `X`; a `lar:` operand compares directly, a relative operand qualifies against each carrier's own scope. The kernel module gate (`tw5-module-gate`) and the HUD pill layer (`lists/components`) ride this surface — typing = running the query (the has-stack law; the retired `implementors` filter's successor).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/source`>>

!! Source

Pure core: `qualifyStackTag` / `stackOf` (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/has-stack.ts`); operator shell: `packages/lararium-tw5/src/filters/stack.ts` (packed into the lares plugin).

